**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`

**How to implement.** Stage 2 (and a joint fit of the same shape) reconstructs each black-box object by the reference linear path, its sessions' gains derived from their AIR runs (001 §L 'per session the gain is free, anchored to its AIR runs, or interpolated between two AIR repeats; dark from the Dark runs'; 001 §L 'the linear path is `MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign` + `reconstruct` (SVD, rank, condition)'; the S11.3 brief 'black-box Mueller objects with calibrated instruments: S10.3's staged path / MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign + reconstruct through MuellerSolverProxy'; step 378's record: 'Deriving an anchored or interpolated session gain from its AIR runs is the staged engine's'). The models are built from the instruments' own (calibrated) values with step 388's constructors, and every row is projected by `projectCaptureRow`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `calibrateLinear` (step 389): (1) `type ParameterValue with member this.airGain : AirGain` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:AirGain`), the number as a detector's gain; `type MuellerMatrix with member this.rowMajorValues : ParameterValue list`, its sixteen elements m00 … m33 row-major (`MuellerMatrix.element`). (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.reconstructLinear (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) : Result<StudyFitSolution, StudyFitError>`, taken only where `engineWith` (step 386) found the black-box shape, over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items` and its layout (step 372). For each fitted run, in study order, over its slots in light order and each item's values `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` (step 245): the source Stokes state and fixed optical matrices MUST come from the same SourceEmission, ItemModelChoice.boundWith, BoundOpticalElement evaluation and per-row dial/orientation/wavelength rules used by the run law (steps 246-252, 258, 367, 374). The incident Stokes vector s MUST fold every fixed matrix before the unknown object; the analyzer row a MUST fold every fixed matrix after it into the detector's S0 row. The object's reference-orientation transforms MUST use effectiveSource and effectiveAnalyzer, with source intensity normalization identical to SourceEmission.emittedInto. This projection MUST work for ideal CP of either handedness, constant-Mueller presets, fixed compounds and fixed surrounding objects without constructing an LP/CPL SourceModel or requiring calibrationPolarizerOpt. its session is the session of `layout.sessions` listing it, its dark `data.darkOf` that session (step 378) or else the detector's `darkOffset` value's `darkMean` (step 374); and its gain MUST follow the session rule at the row's capture time. FreeSessionGain uses the held detector gain; anchored and interpolated rules MUST use each AIR row's actual fixed Stokes/analyzer projection and dark correction with the same gain-ratio arithmetic as airAnchorGainOf from step 388. Factor and call that scalar gain calculation; MUST NOT substitute an LP family for an unsupported fixed optic. Each row MUST produce (s, a, dark-and-gain-corrected intensity) and use LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections, whose designRow is shared with buildDesign (step 388).  The affine runs MUST group by their unknown-bearing object, preserving first-run order; fixed surrounding objects are part of the row projection and MUST NOT become fitted coefficients. Each group's full system MUST reuse LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections. Groups sharing equality-linked leaders MUST be assembled into one reduced system in layout order. An independently reconstructed combined matrix of a series remains a separate diagnostic over that series' rows, never a substitute for either constituent's coefficients. For a single item with all sixteen coefficients free, and for the independently reconstructed combined matrix of a series group, the solve MUST remain `reconstruct solver` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:reconstruct`). For a partly fixed or equality-linked system, resolve each full coefficient to its independent layout leader or a fixed value. Build m = k + P*x, where k holds fixed contributions and P maps independent parameters to their matrix positions. The reduced solve MUST be A*P*x = b - A*k through the injected MuellerSolverProxy.solveLinearLeastSquares. For unlinked unknowns P selects columns, preserving the partial-matrix formula A_U*m_U = b - A_K*m_K. Equality-linked columns MUST be summed, never discarded or solved independently then overwritten. Links across separately observed objects MUST stack their rows into one system using the shared leader column. A link to a fixed leader contributes to k. P and k MUST follow the study's actual link and owner rules; no second parameter-layout implementation is permitted. This MUST reuse `LeastSquaresSystem`, `DesignRow` and the SVD proxy, with no second solver or change to the public `reconstruct` contract. Column selection and reconstruction MUST respect `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerMatrix.vecColumnMajor` (m[row,column] occupies 4*column+row), while fitted entries MUST follow the study layout's order. The solved free values and unchanged fixed values MUST be assembled into a complete sixteen-value vector before `RealVector.columnMajorMueller` is called; a reduced solution MUST NOT be passed directly to that sixteen-value conversion. Fixed KnownParameter and held CalibratedParameter coefficients MUST retain their values exactly and MUST NOT become fitted entries. The returned rank MUST describe the reduced system (15 when only m33 is fixed, 1 when only m00 is free), and rmse MUST describe its corrected measurement residual; rank deficiency MUST be judged against the free-column count by the same solver. Any solver error MUST answer the new `ObjectSolveFitErr of items : ItemId list * error : SolverError`. A group of one item MUST fill only that item's free layout entries from the fitted matrix; every group MUST give one `ObjectMatrixFit { items; elements = matrix.rowMajorValues; rank; rmse }` (step 383) with all sixteen elements, a series group's being the combined matrix S11.4's product check compares with the cascade (001 §L 'the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ)'). The answer is `{ engine = LinearStudyEngine; layout; members = [ { start = <the start values>; outcome = MemberConverged (<the fitted values>, Some <the sum over the groups of rmse² times the group's row count>) } ]; fitted; objectMatrices }`. `SessionGainFitErr` renders `a session gain model was refused: <the error's describe>` and `ObjectSolveFitErr` `the objects could not be reconstructed: <each item id> — <the solver error's describe>`. No weighting, threshold or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over step 389's items with their five instrument parameters published at the truth's constants as `CalibratedParameter`s (step 235), QZ and LR (the black-box model, all sixteen unknown from the identity within [−2, 2]) and the truths M_QZ = `retarderMueller (Angle.degree 30.0<deg>) (Retardance.degree 40.0<deg>)` and M_LR = `retarderMueller (Angle.degree 10.0<deg>) (Retardance.degree 25.0<deg>)` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:retarderMueller`); Science runs of the four families at φ 0°, 30°, 60° and 90° scanning the analyzer dial 0° to 160° by 20°, each row's `avgTotal` g · (`designRow s a` · `M.vecColumnMajor`) + 5 for the projection's s and a; a Dark run of 5; and two hand-set sessions (step 294): `Day 1` anchored to an LP-LP AIR run of gain 1000 (`AnchoredSessionGain`), `Day 2` interpolated between AIR runs of gain 1000 at 10:00 and 1200 at 12:00 (`InterpolatedSessionGain`), its rows generated at the gain the interpolation gives at each row's time: `the object stage reconstructs a black-box matrix behind calibrated instruments, each row divided by its session's gain at its time`: `reconstructLinear` with `createMathNetSvd ()` MUST give QZ's sixteen entries within 1e-9 of M_QZ and one `ObjectMatrixFit` for QZ of rank 16. The same fact MUST also solve three partial variants over those same observations: only m33 held known (15 free), m23 known and m32 held calibrated (14 free, using their distinct signed truth values to expose row/column transposition), and only m00 unknown (1 free). A recording solver proxy MUST delegate to the real `createMathNetSvd ()` and assert the actual reduced column count, column order and right-hand side `b - A_K * m_K` for each variant; this MUST detect a full sixteen-column solve followed by overwriting fixed values. Each result MUST recover the free coefficients within 1e-9, preserve all fixed coefficients exactly, keep fixed coefficients out of fitted entries, return the complete matrix within 1e-9 and report rank equal to the free-column count. All comparisons MUST use the project's tolerance helpers; `a series of two black-box objects is reconstructed as one combined matrix`: with LR's runs and runs of QZ then LR at a shared φ added, LR's entries are within 1e-9 of M_LR and the series' `ObjectMatrixFit` [QZ; LR] holds `cascadeProduct M_LR M_QZ`'s elements within 1e-9; `an object stage whose design is rank-deficient is refused naming its objects`: QZ's runs in the LP-LP family at φ 0° alone MUST answer `ObjectSolveFitErr ([ QZ's id ], RankDeficientErr _)` for both the full matrix and the partial variant with only m33 fixed, after reaching the solver; the partial variant MUST compare rank against its 15 free columns. `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases. Extend the reconstruction fact with (a) only m00 free behind fixed ideal CP of each handedness and a fixed linear analyzer, (b) fixed constant/compound preparation, (c) an unknown matrix between fixed objects, and (d) equality-linked coefficients with observations generated from truth satisfying the links. The recording SVD proxy MUST delegate to createMathNetSvd and assert one column for the m00 case, linked-column sums A*P and target b-A*k, including a fixed leader. The linked fixture MUST include two independently observed objects sharing a leader, so independent per-object solves cannot pass. Recovered independent values MUST meet 1e-9, known values MUST be preserved exactly, linked followers MUST equal their leaders, and rank MUST equal the independent-column count. Source/analyzer projections MUST equal the ordinary run law at each row; no case may pass through an unrelated pre-fit error.

**Acceptance.** After stage 2 lands, `StagedStudy.reconstructLinear` MUST project every capture row of the fitted runs through the fixed instruments' actual item-model matrices, the object angle and the session's dark and gain at the row's time, and solve full object groups by `reconstruct` or a partly fixed single object through the same SVD proxy on `A_U * m_U = b - A_K * m_K`; the partial variants with 15, 14 and 1 free coefficients MUST recover their synthetic truth within 1e-9, preserve every fixed coefficient exactly, report the reduced rank and keep fixed coefficients out of fitted entries, and the reduced rank-deficient case MUST reach the solver and return `ObjectSolveFitErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the object stage reconstructs a black-box matrix behind calibrated instruments, each row divided by its session's gain at its time`, `a series of two black-box objects is reconstructed as one combined matrix` and `an object stage whose design is rank-deficient is refused naming its objects`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass. Fixed ideal-CP, constant/compound optics and fixed surrounding objects MUST reach the real SVD solve. Equality-linked coefficients MUST use combined columns, recover one value per independent leader within 1e-9 and report the independent rank, including cross-object links and fixed leaders.
